t":"B and D"},{"identifier":"C","content":"B and C"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A and C"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"For isothermal process of ideal gas,\n<br><br>PV = constants = K\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>  P = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.829ex\" height=\"2.8ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 808.4 1237.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(232.7,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><rect width=\"568.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n<br><br>So, the graph between P and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.755ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 793.6 1217.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(225.3,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is straight line passing through the origin. So, graph (A) is correct.\n<br><br>As PV = K so the P and V curve is hyperbola. So, graph (B) is wrong.\n<br><br>In isothermal PV = constant.\n<br><br>So, graph (C) is right.\n<br><br>We know internal energy (u) = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.875ex\" height=\"3.006ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -983.5 828.9 1328.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,485) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(237.7,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"588.9\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> nRT. Internal energy is function of temperature (T) only. So, U does not change when volume(V) changes. So, graph (D) is wrong."},"hi":{"content":"ऐसे वक्रों का संयोजन जो एक आदर्श गैस के इसोथर्मल विस्तार का प्रतिनिधित्व नहीं करते हैं – \n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/0C9CF6wnmYkSxIpJW/jSIeof38hWzRQu6CP4vFDuRYVWvHZ/ONi2vemthsd45EyIMdmjA3/im